Based on ONLYOFFICE
-------------------

This program works with ONLYOFFICE Docs, by Ascensio System SIA
(https://www.onlyoffice.com, https://github.com/ONLYOFFICE). ONLYOFFICE is
the original developer of the editor this app runs and of the rules some of
its code carries over.

1. src/locks.ts is a modified version of ONLYOFFICE Docs: the lock rules of
   the server's DocService/sources/DocsCoServer.js (Docs 9.4.0: getLock,
   _checkLockExcel, _checkLockPresentation, compareExcelBlock,
   comparePresentationBlock, _recalcLockArray, _addRecalcIndex,
   CRecalcIndex, and the in-memory editorData's addLocksNX), translated to
   TypeScript and changed to run on a session log instead of a database.
   Modified by BRF Tech on 2026-10-08.
   Portions Copyright (C) Ascensio System SIA. ONLYOFFICE licenses that code
   under the GNU AGPL version 3 only, with additional terms under section 7,
   so this file is AGPL-3.0-only.

2. src/bridge.ts and src/protocol.ts answer the editor in the Document
   Server's protocol (the names and numbers of sdkjs common/docscoapi.js and
   DocsCoServer.js, 9.4), so the editor runs unchanged.

3. The editor files a release bundle will carry (web-apps, sdkjs, the fonts)
   are ONLYOFFICE's, taken from ONLYOFFICE's official Document Server image
   (docker.io/onlyoffice/documentserver) at the release, image tag and
   digest pinned in upstream/onlyoffice.json - today ONLYOFFICE Docs 9.4.0,
   build 9.4.0.129; their source is ONLYOFFICE's sdkjs and web-apps at tag
   v9.4.0.129. The x2t WebAssembly build is ONLYOFFICE's too (ONLYOFFICE
   core). All of it is under ONLYOFFICE's license (AGPL-3.0 with additional
   terms). The bundle will name each with its tag and checksum, keep every
   copyright, license and origin notice they ship, and list here every file
   this project changes, with the date. No release bundle exists yet.

ONLYOFFICE's additional terms (section 7, as rewritten in May 2026) ask that
a modified version:
  - keeps the copyright, license and origin notices;
  - carries a prominent notice, with the dates of the changes, saying it is
    based on ONLYOFFICE by Ascensio System SIA (this file, and the header of
    src/locks.ts);
  - shows, in its interactive interface, an appropriate legal notice that
    names ONLYOFFICE as the original developer, says the version may have
    been modified, and links to the license. The editor's own "About" is
    therefore never hidden, and the app adds this notice where the editor
    opens:

      "This editor is based on ONLYOFFICE Docs by Ascensio System SIA,
       and this version may have been modified. It is free software under
       the GNU Affero General Public License version 3; source code:
       <the exact tag of this repository>."

  - grants no trademark rights: "ONLYOFFICE" is a trademark of Ascensio
    System SIA. This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by or
    sponsored by Ascensio System SIA, and the app does not use the name as
    its own (in filex it is the "Office editor");
  - leaves non-code content (icons, illustrations, documents) under
    CC BY-SA 4.0.
The terms themselves are in ONLYOFFICE's LICENSE files (sdkjs, web-apps,
server, core), which the release bundle will carry unchanged.


The approach
------------

Running ONLYOFFICE's editor in the browser without a Document Server, with
the server's side answered in the editor's frame and the document converted
by x2t built to WebAssembly, is the approach CryptPad takes for its office
documents (https://github.com/cryptpad/cryptpad,
https://github.com/cryptpad/onlyoffice-editor,
https://github.com/cryptpad/onlyoffice-x2t-wasm; AGPL-3.0-or-later). This
project follows that approach; its bridge differs on purpose (the Document
Server's lock and save rules, kept as Docs 9.4 has them).


